Some of the suggestions for modifying spell casting are great.  But I'm
struck that people want to keep "lesser intelligent" characters from
being able to cast the more powerful spells, yet don't complain that
the more intelligent characters can easily "hack-n-slash" with the
best of them.  

Finding gauntlets of power instantly maximizes your strength.  I think 
it should work more like a helm of brilliance.  For crying out loud, even 
if spell casting were made a more integral part of the game as suggested, 
if I had a wizard with strength 25 and a +8 Mjollnir, I wouldn't NEED to 
bother with spells.  I think that modifications need to be made so that a 
wizard MUST rely on wizardry.  As the game stands, I find being a wizard 
easiest.

Neal


